Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.96,0:00:16.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's finished. Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.25,0:00:21.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.08,0:00:22.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.42,0:00:30.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.42,0:00:52.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.46,0:00:55.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is the scientific technique of understanding the structure of matter,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.85,0:00:58.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,decomposing it, and then reconstructing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.70,0:01:05.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If performed skillfully, it is even \Npossible to create gold out of lead.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.46,0:01:12.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, as it is a science, there are some natural principles in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.11,0:01:20.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Only one thing can be created from something else of a certain mass.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.82,0:01:23.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the Principle of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.88,0:01:30.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.40,0:01:31.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Winry!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.96,0:01:35.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Principle of Equivalent Exchange \Nstates that in order to obtain something,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.87,0:01:39.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,something else of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.74,0:01:43.52,Dialogue,,60,0,0,,Is that some kind of maxim?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.52,0:01:48.46,Dialogue,,60,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout sacrificing something?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.76,0:01:52.21,Dialogue,,240,0,0,,Al... Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.62,0:01:54.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alphonse!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.76,0:01:58.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit! I'm not about to let this happen!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.14,0:02:01.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This wasn't... This wasn't supposed to...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.84,0:02:04.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.31,0:02:07.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's been taken away!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.62,0:02:16.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.94,0:02:56.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm starving...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.82,0:03:04.05,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,If only there were some grass growing here, \NI could change it into bread.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.56,0:03:07.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? Al? Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.66,0:03:10.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? Al?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.12,0:03:12.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right here!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.46,0:03:17.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Help me, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.24,0:03:20.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You got buried again?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.54,0:03:25.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do that one more time, \Nand I'm leaving you behind!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.50,0:03:26.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.25,0:03:28.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't "but" me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.14,0:03:33.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.44,0:03:37.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait up, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.48,0:03:39.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not waiting!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.50,0:03:40.87,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.96,0:03:41.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not stopping!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.42,0:03:42.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Straighten up!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.90,0:03:46.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't get buried again!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.30,0:04:05.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.95,0:04:08.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all your fault for not stopping.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.56,0:04:13.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't think anyone would stop \Nif they were told to do so like you did.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.88,0:04:16.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, so that's it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.02,0:04:19.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm so thirsty...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.70,0:04:25.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.28,0:04:26.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.22,0:04:27.28,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.28,0:04:30.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water! Water! Water! \NWater! Water! Water! Water!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.46,0:04:39.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This{\i0} is what I've been smelling all along?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.40,0:04:41.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.05,0:04:45.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blood?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.10,0:04:47.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,More like blood-red wine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.48,0:04:48.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.96,0:04:51.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is off-limits to kids, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.90,0:04:53.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.28,0:04:58.11,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,As travelers, you wouldn't have known that there was wine coming out of there, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.26,0:04:59.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow! Look at that suit of armor!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.11,0:05:01.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The town of Liore here must be pretty prosperous, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.12,0:05:02.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Having a wine fountain and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.61,0:05:06.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you might say that. \NOh, whoops, gotta do this...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.84,0:05:36.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All of God's children, \Nwho live upon this land,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.18,0:05:39.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,pray in faith, that ye may be saved.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.14,0:05:44.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Sun God Leto \Nilluminates thy footsteps.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.11,0:05:45.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.44,0:05:47.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,God, who watches over thee, \Nhas descended from his throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.50,0:05:47.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A religious broadcast?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.92,0:05:51.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and saves thee from all thy sins.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.92,0:05:51.83,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,As far as I'm concerned, I should be the one \Nasking "What's the deal?" of you guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.34,0:05:56.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am Leto's representative, and thy father.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.96,0:05:59.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you guys street performers or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.96,0:05:59.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I offer up this prayer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.34,0:06:03.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now look here, Pop! \NWhere'd you get that idea from?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.30,0:06:06.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're not performers, then what have you come all this way for?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.74,0:06:09.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, there's something we're looking for.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.64,0:06:11.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what's the story with this broadcast?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.98,0:06:13.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's Cornello-sama.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.24,0:06:14.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and like, who is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.34,0:06:17.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't know the representative of the Sun God Leto?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.34,0:06:19.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, so who is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.54,0:06:23.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's Cornello-sama, \Na performer of miraculous works!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.30,0:06:25.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's because of him that this forsaken town in the middle of the desert
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.84,0:06:28.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,has become as prosperous as it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.20,0:06:31.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He really is an incredible man!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.14,0:06:34.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah! The works that man does are truly miraculous!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.95,0:06:37.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not all that interested in religion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.06,0:06:40.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shall we get going, Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.32,0:06:41.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.02,0:06:49.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now you've done it, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.62,0:06:52.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is what happens when you \Ngo around wearing such an outfit!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.00,0:06:54.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, sorry! I'll fix it right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.95,0:06:55.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fix it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.84,0:06:57.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.65,0:06:59.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.66,0:07:00.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.66,0:07:05.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.00,0:07:06.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a transmutation circle.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.62,0:07:07.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.82,0:07:12.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, here goes!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.58,0:07:24.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As the representative of Leto, \NI pour out my love unto thee always.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.64,0:07:27.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a surprise! You guys can also perform miraculous acts?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.60,0:07:28.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you mean by that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.10,0:07:31.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.10,0:07:35.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're the Elric brothers. \NOur reputation is fairly widespread.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.93,0:07:37.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.94,0:07:40.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then it wasn't a miracle?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.06,0:07:43.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've never heard of any alchemists around these parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.38,0:07:47.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's the Fullmetal Alchemist, Edward Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.16,0:07:51.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're famous around East City.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.48,0:07:54.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Said to be an alchemist prodigy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.70,0:07:59.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.22,0:08:00.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.30,0:08:02.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is why your \Nnickname is "Fullmetal"!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.64,0:08:04.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you really that famous? Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.90,0:08:07.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, not me...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.98,0:08:09.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.40,0:08:10.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean the little guy there?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.38,0:08:14.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you calling a bean sprout, too tiny to even notice?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.72,0:08:17.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody called you that!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.90,0:08:20.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Things sure are bustling today!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.70,0:08:24.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Rose!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.67,0:08:28.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, I haven't seen these folks around.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.52,0:08:33.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm Alphonse Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.55,0:08:37.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And I'm the Fullmetal Alchemist, his older brother, Edward Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.62,0:08:40.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh my, {\i1}you're{\i0} the older brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.86,0:08:42.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, now...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.76,0:08:47.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, are you already done shopping for your offering?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.15,0:08:48.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.12,0:08:52.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, take these two along with you to the Church of Leto.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.80,0:08:56.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say they're looking for something, so they could ask for God's grace.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.84,0:08:58.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, but we don't...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.76,0:09:02.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all right. There are \Npilgrim's quarters there too.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.24,0:09:04.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please, make your stay there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.10,0:09:05.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.38,0:09:09.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really? In that case, let's take them up on it, okay, Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.70,0:09:12.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,O-Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.70,0:09:19.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose sure has gotten \Na lot more cheerful, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.50,0:09:22.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. That's thanks to the Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.76,0:09:25.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Especially after what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.32,0:09:34.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.42,0:09:36.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That woman at the shop earlier...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.94,0:09:39.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have we ever seen her before?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.00,0:09:40.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.72,0:09:42.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll be okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.30,0:09:46.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure you'll soon find what you're looking for.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.74,0:09:48.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And what's more...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.54,0:09:51.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you pray, I'm sure you'll grow taller!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.64,0:09:54.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did you say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.55,0:09:56.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go making fun of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.55,0:09:56.30,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.30,0:09:58.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, wait up!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.30,0:09:58.81,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.34,0:10:04.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pray in faith, that thy entreaties may be accorded thee.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.50,0:10:08.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,May all of his children \Nreceive the grace of his light,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.45,0:10:11.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,both today and tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.94,0:10:16.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nicely done, Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.12,0:10:19.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much for your favorable words today.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.54,0:10:22.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.22,0:10:23.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.90,0:10:28.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, may I put some travelers up \Nin the pilgrim's quarters?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.14,0:10:33.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You seem to do all you can each day for God, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.15,0:10:36.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. I serve the Lord Leto always.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.88,0:10:37.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.78,0:10:44.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,God sees your good works.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.26,0:10:48.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason your miracle has not occurred is that the time is still a little too short.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.48,0:10:51.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.28,0:10:58.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? You say that's the grave of Rose-san's beloved?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.30,0:11:02.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Without anyone to rely on, and having lost her boyfriend in an accident,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.58,0:11:06.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose-san clings to \NMinister Cornello's teachings.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.27,0:11:09.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When all the while, there's no way the dead can come back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.66,0:11:11.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They {\i1}do{\i0} appear to come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.78,0:11:15.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As the living are given an immortal soul,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.64,0:11:17.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so are the dead given resurrection.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.04,0:11:21.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The testament is in the \Nmiraculous works, they say.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.48,0:11:25.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sounds fishy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.88,0:11:46.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.18,0:11:50.14,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,There's no two ways about it. \NThat metamorphic reaction must be alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.14,0:11:52.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sure is. But still, the laws—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.60,0:11:54.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, it's you two!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.31,0:11:57.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think about \NCornello-sama's miraculous works?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.86,0:12:00.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how you slice it, \Nthat's alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.00,0:12:02.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This Cornello guy is just a swindling bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.05,0:12:07.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not entirely established. \NWe just know that he's ignoring the laws.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.85,0:12:08.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The laws?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.20,0:12:14.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemy isn't the creation of something out of nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.60,0:12:18.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a scientific technique, \Nwhich obeys the laws of nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.50,0:12:23.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can only get something out of another thing of the same mass.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.72,0:12:27.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like how I could only make a radio that was the same size as before.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.96,0:12:29.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't make it a bigger radio,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.85,0:12:32.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,or change it into a piece of paper, or a tree, or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.69,0:12:37.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's how, if you want to obtain something, you need something of equal value.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.26,0:12:39.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But the old guy up there is disregarding that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.88,0:12:41.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like I've been saying, \Nthey're miracles!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.04,0:12:55.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can you bring about \Nsuch a miracle using alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.50,0:12:59.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And Cain will soon be...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.44,0:13:03.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Elric brothers?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.05,0:13:09.08,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I heard that the older brother received the \Ntitle of State Alchemist when he was twelve.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.08,0:13:11.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's called the Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.14,0:13:13.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That little brat?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.10,0:13:15.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a dog of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.60,0:13:20.08,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,The military has cast their gaze upon our bountiful town here, and plans to intervene.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.08,0:13:24.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The people—my children—must be saved.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.64,0:13:25.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cray...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.72,0:13:28.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I shall carry out the will of God.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.96,0:13:32.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am grateful to you for \Nbringing this to my attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.50,0:13:36.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just having that boy here is troubling, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.42,0:13:40.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is still one other way, \Njust in case.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.78,0:13:53.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just by serving God so dutifully,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.08,0:13:55.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,someone who is dead will \Ncome back to life at some point?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.80,0:13:58.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.98,0:14:11.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water, 35 liters; carbon, 20 kilograms; ammonia, 4 liters; lime, 1.5 kilograms;
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.14,0:14:18.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,phosphorus, 800 grams; salt, 250 grams; saltpeter, 100 grams; sulfur, 80 grams;
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.66,0:14:22.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,fluorine, 7.5 grams; \Niron, 5 grams; silicon, 3 grams;
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.73,0:14:25.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and a small amount of \Nfifteen other elements.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.09,0:14:26.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.48,0:14:32.09,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,That is the material makeup of a single average adult human body if you were to calculate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.66,0:14:35.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Despite being able to know \Nthis much through science,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.49,0:14:39.40,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,there's never been a successful reported case of anyone actually transmuting a human body.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.00,0:14:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For several centuries, scientists have been researching what it is that's missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.36,0:14:49.28,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,Their efforts are more worthwhile than just praying and waiting around, wouldn't you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.42,0:14:52.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, all of these ingredients
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.42,0:14:56.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,can be bought at a market with the spare change any child might have.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.28,0:14:58.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Humans can be made for cheap, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.60,0:15:01.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People aren't things! \NWould you blaspheme God?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.20,0:15:05.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists are scientists,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.17,0:15:09.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so God is something ambiguous, which we don't believe in.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.52,0:15:14.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's ironic, since we're the ones who are closest to being gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.51,0:15:17.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are not a god!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.10,0:15:21.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Neither is the sun. \NIt's just a very hot mass of stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.44,0:15:24.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you get too close to the sun, \Nall you do is burn up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.11,0:15:32.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez, Brother, you're just getting Rose-san upset at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.62,0:15:37.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry. Your brother \Nwill be coming with you soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.38,0:15:45.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Disciple Cray! \NWhat are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.40,0:15:48.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are enemies of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.38,0:15:50.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All of this is God's will!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.10,0:15:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, you startled me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.76,0:16:00.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My head!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.84,0:16:03.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stee-rike!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.78,0:16:05.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?! His head...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.58,0:16:06.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.12,0:16:08.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is how I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.18,0:16:13.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing inside him!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.11,0:16:17.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You could call this the punishment I got \Nfor setting foot on holy ground,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.78,0:16:20.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,which as a person, I should never \Nhave encroached upon. Both me...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.16,0:16:22.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.38,0:16:29.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.06,0:16:35.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's true! It's just like the Minister said!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.42,0:16:38.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Those two are enemies of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.46,0:16:43.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No one ever told us \Nabout this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.23,0:16:48.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.11,0:16:52.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How good of you to \Nbring them here, Rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.06,0:17:02.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A State Alchemist, huh? I had a feeling you would come here sooner or later.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.96,0:17:06.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that because you're a swindler who deceives his believers? Or instead...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.50,0:17:08.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it because you possess the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.94,0:17:11.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.80,0:17:16.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Transmuting without drawing any transmutation circles
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.20,0:17:19.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,while disregarding the\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.40,0:17:21.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There could be only one answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.08,0:17:22.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Quite so.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.49,0:17:27.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The enchanted sorcery amplifier, said to exist only in legend—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.82,0:17:29.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Philosopher's Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.84,0:17:32.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've been looking for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.58,0:17:36.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll get right to the point. \NHand over the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.66,0:17:40.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do that, and I won't say a thing to the people in town.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.03,0:17:43.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean to deprive me of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.34,0:17:47.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If my miraculous works cease, \Nwhat would become of this town?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.98,0:17:50.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right, Rose?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.55,0:17:53.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose! That guy is just \Na third-rate con man!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.70,0:17:58.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I returned life to this town, just as it was about to crumble from internal strife.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.68,0:18:01.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I created water and turned it into wine,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.28,0:18:04.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,built buildings, and even \Ngave money to the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.38,0:18:08.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am the representative of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.34,0:18:13.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you intend to deprive the \Npeople of this city of their God?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.23,0:18:16.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that how absolute the \Norders of the military are?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.07,0:18:19.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't care less \Nabout military orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.58,0:18:20.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.32,0:18:22.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I need...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.20,0:18:24.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We need that thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.20,0:18:26.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.76,0:18:30.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, even knowing it will rob us of hope, are you still after it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.42,0:18:31.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, we're going to—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.92,0:18:32.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.82,0:18:41.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then, why don't we have a look at the power of the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.38,0:18:48.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.68,0:18:52.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your armor has turned against you, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.22,0:18:55.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't very well draw a transmutation circle in that sand, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.96,0:19:14.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Using the Philosopher's Stone, \Nyou synthesized a kindred life form?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.84,0:19:17.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, a Chimera!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.42,0:19:22.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looks like...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.88,0:19:24.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,taking him on barehanded...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.20,0:19:26.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is going to be...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.81,0:19:28.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,tough!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.48,0:19:38.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?! You transmuted without using a transmutation circle?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.92,0:19:47.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go get him!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.36,0:20:11.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How do you like that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.90,0:20:14.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.86,0:20:20.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not getting away!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.59,0:20:40.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter, \Nyou pussy bastard?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.98,0:20:42.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Get yourself a good taste.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.39,0:20:54.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony, that boy...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.04,0:20:59.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-Impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.11,0:21:02.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could his claws not tear through your leg?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.24,0:21:05.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or his fangs crush your arm?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.53,0:21:08.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you're...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.24,0:21:10.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.41,0:21:14.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, take a good look.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.50,0:21:16.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the body of one who performs a human transmutation...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.12,0:21:20.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,of one who encroaches upon God or whoever's territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.91,0:21:24.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is what happens to such transgressors!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.51,0:21:29.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A mechanical... arm and leg? Automail?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.62,0:21:32.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You performed human transmutation?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.80,0:21:35.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've committed that \Nwhich is most sanctioned!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.34,0:21:40.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've had your bodies \Ntaken over to the other side!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.24,0:21:45.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you get too close to the sun, \Nall you do is burn up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.11,0:21:48.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is why your title is "Fullmetal"!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.90,0:21:52.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.22,0:23:40.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.96,0:23:43.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 2: "Body of the Sanctioned"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.94,0:23:45.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A false Philosopher's Stone—
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.50,0:23:49.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it is sure to bring with it \Nfalse peace and false promises.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.92,0:23:53.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, the tears it brings are not false.
